    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25111" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά-λαμψις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shining through,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				369b15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Al.
				<u>T.</u>
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Aeol.
			 and 
				Dor.
			 form of Hellenistic <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάλημψις,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ληψις</span>
			, <i>repute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχειν τινὰ ἐν τᾷ καλλίστᾳ διαλάμψει</span>”
